<!--Post: 4839--><!--Time: 1106769286-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4839"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Marga<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Marga<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 11:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->New poster here, although I&#39;ve been lurking a while... <BR> <BR>Nugster mentioned, in the &#34;BTK 2005&#43; Prediction&#34; thread above, the fact that BTK made the cereal box drop in a rural area. N. wrote: &#34;But notice he did it on a rural road, not in a park or in the city limits. He&#39;s a bit scared. Factor x must wear off when you get old.&#34; <BR> <BR>Do you all agree that maybe BTK avoided making a drop in the city to further avoid being seen? Or does anyone know if there is some significance to the drop spot, geographically-speaking?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4839-->
<!--Post: 4844--><!--Time: 1106770037-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4844"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nancydrew<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nancydrew<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 12:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Marga:  A lot of posters seem to think it was dropped there to hint at BTK&#39;s connection to murders that happened in that area &#40;and were previously unattributed to him&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4844-->
<!--Post: 4845--><!--Time: 1106770094-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4845"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Marga<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Marga<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 12:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Um, responding to my own post, here is Analyzer&#39;s post from the &#34;Delores &#39;Dee&#39; Davis&#34; thread in &#34;Possible BTK Victims&#34;: <BR> <BR>Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 8:25 pm:      <BR> <BR>-------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------ <BR>Updated map  <BR> <BR><a href="http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v622/JMTTS/Wichita7a.jpg" target=_top>http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v622/JMTTS/Wichi ta7a.jpg</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4845-->
<!--Post: 4848--><!--Time: 1106770492-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4848"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Marga<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Marga<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 12:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks, Nancydrew. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4848-->
<!--Post: 4855--><!--Time: 1106777203-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4855"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 2:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>Nugster mentioned, in the &#34;BTK 2005&#43; Prediction&#34; thread above, the fact that BTK made the cereal box drop in a rural area. N. wrote: &#34;But notice he did it on a rural road, not in a park or in the city limits. He&#39;s a bit scared. Factor x must wear off when you get old.&#34;</i> <BR> <BR>I&#39;ll stick with Nugzter&#39;s opinion for now. It&#39;s possible, of course, to hint at other murders, but I want more proof than a cereal box within the vicinity! Let&#39;s see - rather let&#39;s let the police see - <b>detailed drawings, information, trinkets, etc.</b> BTK is cashing in on publicity at the moment, I for one refuse to believe he&#39;s committed any murders for which he hasn&#39;t provided only-the-killer-would-know proof. <BR> <BR>Remember, taking credit for the crimes of others is a classic sociopathic trait. In fact I&#39;m unconvinced BTK has killed anyone except the known victims, and until he provides the same level of minute information he did with Otero, Vian, Fox, Wegerle and Williams, he&#39;s killed no one else, except Kathryn bright, probably.  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4855-->
<!--Post: 4863--><!--Time: 1106779987-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4863"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Marga<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Marga<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 2:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If the authorities find items in the cereal box that link BTK to the unsolved murders in the area, do you think they will release that information to the public?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4863-->
<!--Post: 4865--><!--Time: 1106784287-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4865"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Woody<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Woody<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 4:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t really believe that the drop has anything to do w/ any unsolved murders in the area.  Rather, I believe the old fart is just getting nervous.  I wonder how it feels when the hunter knows he&#39;s being hunted?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4865-->
<!--Post: 4869--><!--Time: 1106785579-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4869"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 4:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Marga - Yes. Not everything would be revealed but the story is too big now to not say anything. It would also be in WPD&#39;s interest to release such information because if they don&#39;t, the press will.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4869-->
<!--Post: 4871--><!--Time: 1106786645-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4871"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Blade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Blade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 4:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, you are dead on, WPD will have to give up information. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4871-->
<!--Post: 5082--><!--Time: 1106865047-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5082"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jim44095<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jim44095<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 2:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m wondering if POST has something to do with this msg board and not cereal but serial killer posting on a board?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5082-->
<!--Post: 5083--><!--Time: 1106866014-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5083"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 2:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree that BTK is using rural drops to stay out of the limelight, so to speak, but something bothers me that I just can not seem to reconcile. <BR> <BR>Granted, his actions seem to suggest that he wants to be careful not to get caught. <BR> <BR>Yet, if that is the case, why not just stop communication altogether?   <BR> <BR>The attention must be a rush for him - but he did without it for a very long time.  That&#39;s where two and two are begining to not add up to four. <BR> <BR>Sometimes I get to wondering if there is not someone &#40;individual or group&#41; that could be benefitting greatly from this attention.  Let&#39;s say a business that sells security systems?  Maybe handguns?   <BR> <BR>Is anyone pulling down some big dollars here?  Because if so - how hard would it be for a sharp guy &#40;or gal&#41; who just happened to befriend &#40;go into business with..&#41; a dectective from the original BTK investigation - or records clerk, what have you, and come up with an extremely successful ploy? <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5083-->
<!--Post: 5160--><!--Time: 1106931662-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5160"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 9:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><b><i>Sometimes I get to wondering if there is not someone &#40;individual or group&#41; that could be benefitting greatly from this attention. Let&#39;s say a business that sells security systems? Maybe handguns?</i></b> <BR> <BR>If these drops are all an elaborate hoax, how could the perpetrator ensure that the public went rushing to his alarm system business or gun shop? I&#39;m willing to bet there are plenty of either type of business in and around the city of Wichita.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5160-->
<!--Post: 6582--><!--Time: 1107901091-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6582"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Crimone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Crimone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 2:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just a thought that has been nagging at me...What if the circle around the T on the Post Toasties box represents the necklace? Like BTK told Tom to &#34;look between the clues to locate him&#34; &#40;or something to that effect&#41;. Someone suggested the brick may indicate &#34;following the yellow brick road.&#34; If the circle represents the necklace, then perhaps the necklace could be located at the nearest T of that rural area? Just an idea...may be way off...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6582-->
<!--Post: 6583--><!--Time: 1107901164-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6583"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Crimone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Crimone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 2:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->More correctly, &#34;around&#34; the nearest T.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6583-->
<!--Post: 6660--><!--Time: 1107929499-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6660"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 10:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK is feeling the heat and avoiding taking chances of detection. He &#40;If Tom believes him, I believe him&#41; has posted, on his string, hinting at his next &#39;strike&#39;, possibly &#39;something about when a rooster crows&#39;, which would suggest a rural setting in the morning. Aside from extending the terror territory he might be trying to spread the police thin and finish his book/project before they catch him. <BR> <BR>As far as the necklace goes, I would be surprised if he let it out of his possession without placing it in someone elses.  <BR> <BR>6 days to Valentines Day though...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6660-->
<!--Post: 6711--><!--Time: 1107973086-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6711"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lctrip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lctrip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 10:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bmodule - certainly the rural setting fits the comment about &#34;when the rooster crows&#34;, however something else to think about.....  Today &#40;Feb 9th&#41; is Chinese New Year - this year is the year of the rooster, so in effect today the rooster crows on the dawning of a new &#40;Chinese&#41; year. <BR> <BR>Now the fact that today is Chinese New Year is pretty common knowledge in many cities here on the West Coast because of the large contingent of Asians, but Kansas?!  Perhaps it&#39;s more diverse than I remember. <BR> <BR>Just a thought, for what it&#39;s worth.....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6711-->
<!--Post: 6820--><!--Time: 1108020263-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6820"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 11:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks for post...you just gave me a thought. See &#34;Feedback to messages from BTK&#34;. I will post it there.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6820-->
